<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 10.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 10.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period April 8 to 10.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 8 (actual) 213 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 9 (forecast) 205 mcm, 48 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 10 (forecast) 199 mcm, 46 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 8 (actual) 10.0 Celsius, SNT 8.8 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 9 (forecast) 11.0 Celsius, SNT 8.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 10 (forecast)11.0 Celsius, SNT 9.0 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on Wednesday, with none expected on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
